// R19.schema, the OLD side of the Go conformance row R19's committed pair
// (test/conformance/go/rows/R19_test.go). R19's law: "a clean NEW-READS-OLD
// of an appended field, variant, arm, flag or keyed slot moves no counter at
// all" (docs/roadmap.sexp, go/R19).
//
// The pair differs by EXACTLY ONE definition change: ../new/R19.schema appends
// one field, w, at the end of the table. Both sides keep the package tblr19
// because the two layouts are ONE LINEAGE (../new/schema.lock carries this
// side's layout as its lineage entry); the build generates each side into its
// own module, tblr19old and tblr19new (make/go.mk), and the row imports them
// under aliases. ../old.bin is this side's writer's file.
package tblr19

fixed table Reading
{
    x int32 = 0
    y int32 = 0
    z int32 = 0
}
